        <item>
            <title>2.14.3</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 11:38:48 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>86</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.14.3</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Bug Fixes

- **The close button on a pane header now works.** It never did — macOS 26 lays a backdrop over the top of the detail column that swallows clicks before they reach the button, so the X was inert from the day multi-pane split view shipped. The click is now handled directly, ahead of that backdrop.

### Changes

- **The pane close button is always visible**, instead of appearing only on hover. A New Session pane has no sidebar row of its own, so a hidden — and unclickable — X left it with no way to close it at all: ⌘W acts on the focused pane, and the sidebar can only show that *a* New Session pane is focused, never which one.

### Known limitations

Two clicks on the close X do more than a normal button would, and are deliberately left as-is for now:

- Ctrl-clicking or ⌘-clicking the X closes the pane, rather than opening a context menu or acting as ⌘-click does elsewhere.
- Clicking the X on a Canopy window that is in the background closes the pane as well as bringing the window forward.

Closing a pane never closes the session behind it, so the cost either way is re-opening a pane.
]]></description>
